lue":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T20:36:39-07:00","id":1561018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560442-new-vtm-game-eternal-whispers?p=1561012#post1561012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily, I'd like a source for that, not just reasoning.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat doesn't want to prevent Gehenna, they want to <b><i>win </i></b>it. And they want to spite the Camarilla, who actually fears Gehenna and tries to prevent it killing thin bloods while pretending not to.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no &quot;winning&quot; Gehenna, because it's not a war. Its a doomsday scenario that foretells the extinction of vampires as a species.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat may be crazy, but they're not brain damaged. They are fully aware that a direct confrontation against the Antedeluvians would be suicide. Every time just one of these things have been taken out, it came at the expense of a small army of vampires and ghouls working round the clock, just to whittle down their defenses.<br /> <br /> The plan was to hunt down the Antedeluvians in their resting places and slay them BEFORE they woke up and started eating everybody. With them gone, the Sabbat would then be free to reign over the earth without the threat of 13 blood gods looming over them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> From what people are saying on Steam, that game is not taking place in 5th edition. Which means we can disregard whatever stupidity the V5 Sabbat are involved with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T23:34:06-07:00","id":1561020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560442-new-vtm-game-eternal-whispers?p=1561018#post1561018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> From what people are saying on Steam, that game is not taking place in 5th edition. Which means we can disregard whatever stupidity the V5 Sabbat are involved with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well apparently some events of V5 has happened since the church hq is in ruins. Now it could just be the game devs putting they own spin on 5e lore like what Purgatory did with the whole thing with the mother/farther wolf split. <br /> <br /> Of course a more intresting approach would be a preview of a playable sabbat for v6...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T00:51:41-07:00","id":1561023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560442-new-vtm-game-eternal-whispers?p=1561018#post1561018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no &quot;winning&quot; Gehenna, because it's not a war. Its a doomsday scenario that foretells the extinction of vampires as a species.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's conflating different accounts.<br /> <br /> Gehenna is a prophecised awakening of the Antes followed by their attack. The prophecy states this will spell doom over all vampires.<br /> <br /> But the Sabbat has its own spin on it: instead of reading it as a guaranteed loss, they plan to change things by killing the Antes. They are not picky about the method, even if they obviously prefer to do it during their sleep.<br /> <br /> Preventing Gehenna is a Camarilla thing. For the Sabbat it isn't preventable, it's winnable through initiative.<br /> <br /> I'll see later if I can confirm this from actual official sources. The whole point of the Sabbat includes a distinct attitude and interpretation of prophecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T03:08:39-07:00","id":1561072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560442-new-vtm-game-eternal-whispers?p=1561018#post1561018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no &quot;winning&quot; Gehenna, because it's not a war. Its a doomsday scenario that foretells the extinction of vampires as a species.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat may be crazy, but they're not brain damaged. They are fully aware that a direct confrontation against the Antedeluvians would be suicide. Every time just one of these things have been taken out, it came at the expense of a small army of vampires and ghouls working round the clock, just to whittle down their defenses.<br /> <br /> The plan was to hunt down the Antedeluvians in their resting places and slay them BEFORE they woke up and started eating everybody. With them gone, the Sabbat would then be free to reign over the earth without the threat of 13 blood gods looming over them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> From what people are saying on Steam, that game is not taking place in 5th edition. Which means we can disregard whatever stupidity the V5 Sabbat are involved with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the Sabbat! Ever heard of Gehenna War? <br /> <br /> Sabbat is a doomsday cult but also a fanatic religious army. They believe that when Gehenna comes Antediluvians will awaken and then Caine will come to judge the Cainites. So their idea is to kill Caine's grandchilder who strayed from the grandfather's commandments and believe in doing so achieve the absolution from the Dark Father. <br /> <br /> You should remember that the actions of vampires, like actions of people are rarely the reason of logical thinking. Emotions rule vampires as strongly, sometimes more so, as people. And it's easier for powerful Cainite to manipulate his lesser than for the social media. Also, we are still talking about a group of religious fanatics? You might think it brain damage but they consider it part of dogma. Want to be Ancient pawn? Join the Camarilla. Stay Sabbat if you want to be a proud Caine warrior. Or at least that's the propaganda. <br /> <br /> But yes, in previous editions Sabbat was gung ho about killing Thin-bloods but in V5 it will gladly use them as shovelheads and use and abuse their unique powers in their fight. <br /> <br /> As for the game? I would not read to much into it, writers will take whatever idea they like, and disregard whatever does not fit the story they want to tell, from the source material. It has been true of every previous VtM video game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T08:17:09-07:00","id":1561076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560442-new-vtm-game-eternal-whispers?p=1561072#post1561072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should remember that the actions of vampires, like actions of people are rarely the reason of logical thinking. Emotions rule vampires as strongly, sometimes more so, as people. And it's easier for powerful Cainite to manipulate his lesser than for the social media. Also, we are still talking about a group of religious fanatics? You might think it brain damage but they consider it part of dogma.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not brain damage or lack of logic, anyway.<br /> <br /> Ambiguity, uncertainty, is part of the game. The stance is weird if you take standard prophecy as a fact, but it's not.<br /> <br /> The usual prophecy may be right. The Sabbat may be right. The Setites may be right. Bahari, Laibon, Werewolves, Changelings.<br /> <br /> While you may take any as headcanon and treat the others as disillusioned fools, the game is built so the truth may be close to any, or be something else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T14:12:40-07:00","id":1561111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-wo